%% Statechart of AskRefusal.tla for one call under design "a" (the pick).
%% Rule breaks on origin/main ("today") are noted on the states they break.
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Idle
  Idle --> Reviewing: shell call starts (Begin)
  Idle --> Reviewing: file target reaches its check (Review)
  Idle --> Refusing: hook or bad arguments block it (Refuse)
  Reviewing --> Reviewing: auto review starts, one Reviewing line (StartReview)
  Reviewing --> Held: auto review holds the call (Hold)
  Reviewing --> Admitted: review or permission admits a run (Admit)
  Reviewing --> Refusing: configured deny, no terminal, file deny (Refuse)
  Held --> Refusing: held call is refused (Refuse)
  Held --> Admitted: fresh review clears the held call (Admit)
  Idle --> Cancelled: you cancel (Cancel)
  Reviewing --> Cancelled: you cancel (Cancel)
  Held --> Cancelled: you cancel (Cancel)
  Admitted --> Cancelled: you cancel (Cancel)
  Refusing --> Closed: record written, refusal printed once (Close)
  Admitted --> Closed: run finishes, no reason (Close)
  Cancelled --> Closed: record written, no refusal line (Close)
  Closed --> [*]

  note right of Reviewing
    Design a: a reviewed call prints one "Reviewing <tool>: <summary>" line when
    its review starts, then nothing until its final line. The Running line is held.
    A call the rules allow with no review prints no Reviewing line.
    Today: Running is written here, before admission (breaks NoRunningForRefused).
    Today: no Reviewing line at all (breaks ReviewTold).
  end note
  note right of Held
    Design a: the hold prints nothing; the Reviewing line printed at review start.
  end note
  note right of Refusing
    Design a: one "Refused <tool>: <reason>" line, reason in --json.
    Today: no line, no reason (breaks RefusalTold and JsonReason).
  end note
  note right of Cancelled
    Today: a Running line already on stderr stays there (breaks NoRunningForRefused).
  end note
